ead 2-1 with 17 seconds left when Monday made a crotch lift reversal to tie the match, which went into overtime. Early in the extra period Monday grabbed Varayev in a body lock and took him down for 3 points which turned out to be the margin of victory. Monday would compete at the 1992 and 1996 Olympics, winning a silver medal in 1992 and placing sixth in 1996. Varayev retired from competition after Seoul and became a coach."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Round Eliminated"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Classification Points", :class "footnote"} "CP"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/60715"} "Kenny Monday"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "9"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/60554"} "Adlan Varayev"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "25"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/57464"} "Rahmat Sofiadi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/BUL"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/BUL.png"}] "BUL"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {:class "bib"} "18"] [:td {} [:a {:hr